Вы молотцы.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.540
Now, let's talk a little bit about grammar.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.600
But don't worry, we'll keep it simple and friendly.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.520
In Russian, every noun has a gender.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:42.020
Маскулин, феменин, or neuter.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.220
Even objects like rockets and moons have gender.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:50.680
Most nouns that end in A or Y are feminine.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:05:01.500
So rakieta, феменин, планета, феменин, звезда, феменин, Луна, феменин.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.620
Most nouns that end in a consonant are masculine.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:13.120
So, космос, маскулин, спутник, маскулин.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.980
That's why we say красивая rakieta.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.060
Beautiful rocket, feminine.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:21.900
Красивый спутник, beautiful satellite, masculine.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.620
Красивая Луна, beautiful moon, feminine.

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.620
If you can notice these small changes,

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.180
you are already doing real Russian grammar.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:34.480
Amazing, right?

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:38.300
Russians are incredibly proud of their space history.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:42.440
In Tissiccia, деветсот шестьдесят один.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:43.980
Russian космонот.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.740
Юрий Гагарин became the very first person to fly into space.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.360
He orbited the Earth in a tiny capsule called Vostok 1.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.700
When he came back, he was a hero all over the world.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:03.700
Even today, many Russian children dream of becoming cosmonauts.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:08.260
In Russian culture, space stands for big dreams, courage, friendship,

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:12.000
and the belief that if people work together, nothing is impossible.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.200
That's why you will often hear Russian say,

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:20.200
в период гзвездом, it means forward to the stars.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.680
Now here's something really cool.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.560
My favorite secret about one of today's words.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:30.840
Do you want to know the hidden story of the word Sputnik?

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.720
Long before it meant satellite,

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.140
Sputnik came from all church Slavonic.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:40.260
It literally means fellow traveler

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.820
or the one who travels with you.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.940
It's made from two parts.

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.120
So, meaning with and put meaning path.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:54.260
In Tissiccia, деветсот пятьдесят сидмом.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.580
The Soviet Union launched the very first artificial satellite.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.580
They named it Sputnik-Down-1.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:07.440
Suddenly newspapers all over the world were using the Russian word Sputnik.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:12.080
English borrowed it, so now English has two words.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:16.560
satellite and Sputnik that are almost the same.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.340
But here's the fun part.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:23.080
In everyday Russian, Sputnik can also mean a traveling companion

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:28.060
or even your boyfriend or girlfriend in a sweet old fashioned way.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:34.060
So, satellite orbiting Earth and your best friend are both called Sputnik.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:39.320
Next time you hear the word Sputnik, remember it's not just a space word.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:44.460
It's your secret memory hook that means the thing that travels together with you.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:47.740
That connection will help you remember the word forever.

